### Requests for the IntelliJ / VS Code "REST Client" extension. Start the app with profile "local" first.

### 1. Get a token (local profile only)
POST http://localhost:8080/dev/token

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. Small payment (Ben -> Shop) -> COMPLETED automatically
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-payment-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorIban": "DE02120300000000202051",
  "creditorIban": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "remittanceInfo": "Order 4711"
}

### 3. Same key, same body again -> 200 with the SAME payment (idempotent replay)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-payment-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorIban": "DE02120300000000202051",
  "creditorIban": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "remittanceInfo": "Order 4711"
}

### 4. High amount (Anna) -> PENDING_REVIEW, approve in Tasklist (demo/demo)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-payment-002
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorIban": "DE89370400440532013000",
  "creditorIban": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 15000.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 5. Not enough money (Ben has 1,000 EUR) -> REJECTED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-payment-003
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "debtorIban": "DE02120300000000202051",
  "creditorIban": "DE75512108001245126199",
  "amount": 9999.00,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 6. CSV import from a partner
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/payments/import
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: text/csv

< ./samples/payments.csv
